.TH PVE-KLP 8 "2026-11-23" "pve-klp 0.1.5" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pve-klp \- verify and load kernel livepatches on Proxmox VE hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve-klp
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve-klp
fetches the signed livepatch manifest for exactly the running kernel,
verifies it, loads the livepatch module and watches the livepatch
transition. A stalled transition is reversed, never forced. If a new
level misbehaves after its transition, it is disabled and the previous
level is restored from the local cache.
.PP
A livepatch bridges the time until the next maintenance window. It does
not replace installing the kernel update and rebooting.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fB\-\-repository \fIurl\fR] [\fB\-\-ring \fIring\fR] [\fB\-\-key \fIfile|url\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-name \fIname\fR]
Write repository and ring into the configuration file, install the
manifest signing key into the trusted key directory, print its key id
and run
.BR check .
Options that are not given keep the value already configured;
.B \-\-repository
is required the first time, the ring defaults to
.BR stable .
Every value is printed with what changed.
Compare the printed key id with the one published by the repository
owner.
.TP
.B check \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Check prerequisites: kernel configuration, ftrace, module loading,
Secure Boot and MOK enrollment, trusted keys, repository reachability,
foreign or forced livepatches and active kprobes.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show the running kernel, the active livepatch level, the CVEs fixed live
and the CVEs that still need a reboot.
.TP
.B apply \fR[\fB\-\-level \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-replace\-foreign\fR]
Fetch, verify and load the livepatch for the running kernel. With
.BR \-\-level ,
only apply if the repository offers exactly level
.IR N .
With
.BR \-\-replace\-foreign ,
allow atomic replace to disable livepatches not built by this project.
.TP
.B boot
Reload the previously active level for the running kernel from the
local cache, without network access. Run by
.BR pve-klp-boot.service .
.TP
.B revert
Disable and unload the active livepatch and put the node on hold:
neither the timer nor the boot unit loads a livepatch again, and the
timer does not contact the repository, until the next explicit
.BR apply .
An explicit
.B apply
always evaluates the repository; the hold ends when it loads a level.
.TP
.B auto enable\fR|\fBdisable
Enable or disable
.BR pve-klp-auto.timer ,
which runs
.B apply
hourly. Disabled by default.
.TP
.B mok enroll
Import the module signing certificate as Machine Owner Key. Confirm the
enrollment in MokManager on the console during the next boot.
.B mokutil
asks for a one-time password on the terminal; it does not read it from a
pipe.
.SH VERIFICATION
Before loading,
.B pve-klp
checks the minisign signature of the manifest against the trusted keys,
the kernel release and the vmlinux build-id, the release ring, the
expiry date, that the level is not lower than any level accepted before
(also after
.BR revert ),
the SHA-256 of the module, and its
.IR livepatch ,
.I name
and
.I vermagic
module information. The kernel verifies the module signature itself.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B status:
0 livepatch active, no known CVE needs a reboot;
10 active, but a reboot is required;
11 no livepatch active;
12 manifest expired;
20 last operation failed or transition in progress.
.PP
.BR apply ,
.BR boot ,
.BR revert :
0 applied, already active, nothing published or on hold;
2 failed and backed out;
3 rejected by verification or policy, nothing loaded;
4 precondition failed;
1 other error.
.PP
systemd labels exit codes of units with LSB names (2 INVALIDARGUMENT,
3 NOTIMPLEMENTED, 4 NOPERMISSION). For
.B pve-klp
they mean only what is listed above; for example a rejected rollback in
.B pve-klp-auto.service
shows up as status=3/NOTIMPLEMENTED.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pve-klp/pve-klp.toml
Configuration. Created from
.I /usr/share/pve-klp/pve-klp.toml
on installation when missing; package upgrades never change it.
.TP
.I /etc/pve-klp/trusted.d/*.pub
Trusted manifest signing keys (minisign format).
.TP
.I /etc/pve-klp/hooks.d/
Executables run, in name order, after each successful load by
.B apply
or the boot reload (not after
.BR revert ),
with
.BR PVE_KLP_KERNEL ,
.B PVE_KLP_LEVEL
and
.B PVE_KLP_MODULE
set. A non-zero exit reverts the livepatch.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pve-klp/
State and module cache.
.TP
.I /var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter/pve_klp.prom
Metrics for the node_exporter textfile collector.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PVE_KLP_CONFIG
Alternative configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR mokutil (1),
.BR modinfo (8)
.PP
https://github.com/prepaid-host/pve-klp
